<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">White Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1963</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The White Revolution was a programme of reforms launched by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-reza-pahlavi">Mohammad Reza Shah</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-persian">Pahlavi</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and approved by referendum in January 1963. It included land reform, the sale of state factories, profit-sharing for workers, a literacy corps and votes for women. It weakened landlords and clergy, and opposition to it brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhollah-khomeini">Ruhollah Khomeini</a> to prominence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/white-revolution.jpg" alt="White Revolution" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mrplandreform1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
